                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient shows mildly elevated total cholesterol and triglycerides, while LDL cholesterol remains within the normal range. These findings suggest a moderate dyslipidemia, which may increase cardiovascular risk, especially at advanced age. Clinical correlation and consideration of lipid-lowering therapy or lifestyle modification may be warranted.</td>
